  "sites": [
    {
      "id": "3:1",
      "quote": "In this case, the initiator MUST verify that payload and any associated certificates, as per [RFC4306].",
      "disposition": "mapped",
      "mapped-to": "RFC5998-3-1"
    },
    {
      "id": "3:2",
      "quote": "When receiving message 4, the initiator MUST verify that the proposed EAP method is allowed by this specification, and MUST abort the protocol immediately otherwise.",
      "disposition": "mapped",
      "mapped-to": "RFC5998-3-2"
    },
    {
      "id": "3:3",
      "quote": "Both the initiator and responder MUST verify that the EAP method actually used provided mutual authentication and established a shared secret key.",
      "disposition": "mapped",
      "mapped-to": "RFC5998-3-3"
    },
    {
      "id": "3:4",
      "quote": "The AUTH payloads sent after EAP Success MUST use the EAP-generated key, and MUST NOT use SK_pi or SK_pr (see Section 2.15 of [RFC5996]).",
      "disposition": "mapped",
      "mapped-to": "RFC5998-3-4"
    },
    {
      "id": "3:5",
      "quote": "Therefore, during the IKE_AUTH exchange of the resumed session, this extension MUST NOT be sent by the initiator.",
      "disposition": "mapped",
      "mapped-to": "RFC5998-3-5"
    },
    {
      "id": "4:1",
      "quote": "EAP methods to be used with this extension MUST have the following properties:",
      "disposition": "mapped",
      "mapped-to": "RFC5998-4-1"
    },
    {
      "id": "6.1:1",
      "quote": "Thus, EAP methods that do not provide mutual authentication or establish a shared secret key MUST NOT be used with the modifications presented in this document.",
      "disposition": "excluded",
      "excluded-kind": "duplicate-of",
      "reason": "restates the Section 3 rule that the EAP method used must provide mutual authentication and a shared secret key",
      "mapped-to": "RFC5998-3-3"
    },
    {
      "id": "6.2:1",
      "quote": "These AAA proxies MUST be trusted for secure operation, and therefore SHOULD be avoided when possible; see Section 2.3.4 of [RFC4072] and Section 4.3.7 of [RFC3579] for more discussion.",
      "disposition": "excluded",
      "excluded-kind": "binds-another-role",
      "reason": "AAA deployment operator: the sentence obliges whoever places AAA proxies between the IKEv2 gateway and the backend AAA server to trust them; no IKEv2 implementation, ze's included, chooses or vets the AAA path"
